    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0850" n="1808" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1808"/>

                <head>No. 45.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Garland to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 31, 1888</date>.
                        (Received June 1.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 29th instant, inclosing a copy of a memorandum from the
                    British minister, in relation to the cases of seizure of British vessels in
                    Behring Sea, and to say that I know of no mode remaining by which the decrees of
                    condemnation can be reviewed.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. H. Garland.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
